# Allen Relation: OVERLAPS / OVERLAPPED-BY
#
# OVERLAPS: A starts, then B starts before A ends, then A ends while B continues.
#   A overlaps B  iff  A.start < B.start < A.end < B.end
#
# OVERLAPPED-BY: the symmetric inverse.
#   B overlapped-by A  iff  B.start > A.start and B.start < A.end and B.end > A.end
#
# Legal patterns that trigger OVERLAPS:
#   "whilst awaiting the completion of necessary procedures"
#   "applied provisionally from X" while old agreement still nominally in force
#   "pending entry into force, the parties agree to apply"
#   "during the transition period" where two regimes coexist
#   amendment applied before old agreement formally terminated
#
# Grounded example (en_contracts_seed1):
#   Original agreement [1986-07-19, formal_termination) OVERLAPS
#   amended agreement provisional period [1995-01-01, entry_into_force).
#   Original starts first, amended starts before original ends,
#   original ends while amended continues.

```catala
declaration scope AllenOverlaps:
  input interval_a_start content date   # start of the first period
  input interval_a_end content date     # end of the first period
  input interval_b_start content date   # start of the overlapping period
  input interval_b_end content date     # end of the overlapping period
  output is_overlaps content boolean    # A starts before B, B starts before A ends
  output is_overlapped_by content boolean  # B started earlier, A started during B
```

## OVERLAPS

A starts before B, B starts before A ends, A ends before B ends.

```catala
scope AllenOverlaps:
  date round down
  definition is_overlaps equals
    (interval_a_start < interval_b_start) and
    (interval_b_start < interval_a_end) and
    (interval_a_end < interval_b_end)
```

## OVERLAPPED-BY

The symmetric inverse: B started first, A started during B, B ends before A.

```catala
scope AllenOverlaps:
  definition is_overlapped_by equals
    (interval_b_start < interval_a_start) and
    (interval_a_start < interval_b_end) and
    (interval_b_end < interval_a_end)
```
